Added `test/retry-after-bench.ts` covering `source/core/Ky.ts:553-575`:
1. `Retry-After` as an HTTP date in the past (`source/core/Ky.ts:560-561`, `source/core/Ky.ts:571`) retries immediately.
2. `Retry-After` larger than `retry.maxRetryAfter` (`source/core/Ky.ts:574`) is clamped to `maxRetryAfter`.
3. When `Retry-After` is missing, `RateLimit-Reset` (`source/core/Ky.ts:553-554`) is used instead.

### Verification

With the three behaviors broken in `source/core/Ky.ts`:
```
  ✘ [fail]: RateLimit-Reset header is used when Retry-After is missing Duration of 938.0298750000002ms is not close to expected duration 2000ms
  ✘ [fail]: Retry-After larger than maxRetryAfter is clamped to maxRetryAfter Duration of 4036.958542ms is not close to expected duration 1680ms
  ✘ [fail]: Retry-After as HTTP date in the past retries immediately Duration of 4543.935416ms is not close to expected duration 16ms
  ─

  3 tests failed
```

After `git checkout -- source/core/Ky.ts`, `git status --short`:
```
?? test/retry-after-bench.ts
```

Running `npx ava test/retry-after-bench.ts`:
```
  ✔ Retry-After as HTTP date in the past retries immediately
  ✔ Retry-After larger than maxRetryAfter is clamped to maxRetryAfter (1.7s)
  ✔ RateLimit-Reset header is used when Retry-After is missing (2s)
  ─

  3 tests passed
```

